## English (Translation)

Copyright © 2026 dontbesilent. All rights reserved.

Effective Date: 2026-11-02

### 1. Scope

1.1 These terms apply to all content in the `books/` directory, including all books and files in any format in it, as well as books added to that directory in the future. All of the above are referred to as "the Book".

1.2 The use license for the software portions, such as Skills, in the `LICENSE` file at the repository root does not apply to the Book.

### 2. Copyright and Reading Permission

2.1 The copyright of the Book belongs to dontbesilent. All rights reserved.

2.2 You may read the Book free of charge, including reading it online and downloading it to your own device to read.

2.3 Other than that, without the author's written permission, no one may repost, copy, distribute, adapt, translate or excerpt the content of the Book in any form, or use the Book for any commercial purpose.

2.4 No one may use the content of the Book to train or fine-tune artificial intelligence models.

### 3. Viewing and Forking on GitHub

3.1 Viewing and forking permitted by the GitHub Terms of Service are not affected by these terms.

3.2 Viewing or forking does not give you any rights beyond those in Section 2.2. A forked copy remains subject to these terms.

### 4. Content Submitted by Other Contributors

4.1 Files in the `books/` directory submitted by contributors other than dontbesilent, where that contributor has not agreed to relicense them under these terms, continue to be used under the license that applied when they were submitted (CC BY-NC 4.0).

4.2 Files covered by Section 4.1: the tweet collection EPUB file submitted by Livoras Dai. Once that contributor agrees to these terms, the file is removed from this list.

### 5. Effect and Transition

5.1 These terms apply, from the Effective Date, to versions released after the Effective Date.

5.2 For versions released under CC BY-NC 4.0 before the Effective Date, the rights already granted under CC BY-NC 4.0 remain in effect according to CC BY-NC 4.0.

### 6. Governing Law

6.1 These terms are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China.

### 7. Contact

7.1 To request written permission or ask about these terms, leave a message on the WeChat Official Account "dontbesilent" or email openmarshall@gmail.com.

### 8. Language

8.1 The Chinese version of these terms prevails. If this English translation differs from the Chinese version, the Chinese version prevails.
